    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's more than just feeling lost though. it feels like the fog isnt something i can walk out of. it's more like the ground itself is just gone. when i look ahead, there's no more forest, no more trail, just this quiet, empty space. it feels so much more peaceful looking at that emptiness than trying to struggle through the grey forever. like the story has just naturally reached its final page.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
